# Test Plan — E-Commerce Checkout Flow

## 1. Objective
Validate that the checkout flow of a demo e-commerce web application works correctly end to end: cart review, shipping details, payment, and order confirmation — across happy paths, validation rules, and edge cases.

## 2. Scope
**In scope**
- Cart review page (items, quantities, totals)
- Shipping information form and validation
- Promo/discount code application
- Payment form (test card numbers) and error handling
- Order confirmation page and confirmation email

**Out of scope**
- Account registration / login flows
- Admin/order-management backend
- Performance and load testing
- Real payment gateway processing (test mode only)

## 3. Test types
- Functional testing (each checkout step)
- Input validation & negative testing
- Regression testing (after fixes)
- Exploratory testing (edge cases: double-clicks, back button, session timeout)
- Basic usability checks (error message clarity, mobile layout)

## 4. Test environment
- Browsers: latest Chrome, Firefox, Safari
- Desktop + one mobile viewport (iPhone)
- Test card numbers provided by the payment sandbox

## 5. Entry criteria
- Checkout build deployed to the test environment
- Test data ready (products in catalog, valid/invalid/declined test cards, promo codes)

## 6. Exit criteria
- All planned test cases executed
- No open Critical/High severity defects
- All High-priority defects retested and closed

## 7. Schedule (sample)
| Phase | Duration |
|---|---|
| Test design | 2 days |
| Test execution — round 1 | 3 days |
| Defect retesting & regression | 2 days |

## 8. Risks
- Payment sandbox downtime → use documented fallback test cards
- Last-minute UI changes → prioritize smoke test of the happy path first
